# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep secrets out of it.
# A file that never enters the context cannot end up in an image layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.git/
.github/
docs/
tests/
db/
scripts/
infra/
*.md
# ...except the one the workspace root pyproject declares as its readme.
# Excluding it makes the build fail at metadata parse time, some distance from
# the line that actually caused it.
!README.md
# ...and the sleep cycle's prompts, which are runtime data the image reads via
# importlib.resources, not documentation. A blanket *.md rule silently
# dropping these would build successfully and fail only once deployed, when
# resources.files(...).read_text() raises inside a cold-starting Lambda — see
# services/sleep-cycle/src/mnemos_sleep_cycle/distill.py.
!services/sleep-cycle/src/mnemos_sleep_cycle/prompts/*.md
